-- title:
--   Element of y outside (U,varpi) at a crossing end
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Fixed are: a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero; an element $\xi \in L$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; and the hypothesis `hι` that some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carries $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Further, $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which by `hK` equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79): the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H(N_0)$, where $N_0 = (q\ell)^2M'$ and $H =$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Next, $A$ is a Henselian discrete valuation ring which is an $L$-algebra with $L$ as its fraction field, with algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`); $K$ carries a compatible $A$-algebra structure. The element $j \in K$ is nonzero and has Laurent expansion the coefficient embedding of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function), $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Throughout, $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` denotes the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A ↥K j` is $j$ viewed in $C$.
--
--   **The supersingular point.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of $C$ containing $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), and `hss` requires: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **Local rigidity at supersingular points (`hArig`).** This hypothesis asserts, for every point $z$ of the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (pulled back from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ along `toBase`) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` whose prime ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as in `hss`, the existence of: a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ ([`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) being $X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v - f\,u\bigr)$, subject to seven clauses (summarised here): $e$ sends the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; the level automorphisms $\tau$ of $K/L$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ — those satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), i.e. acting on ratios of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with integral $q$-expansions by the substitution `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` after any embedding of $L$ into $\mathbb{C}$ matching $\xi$ with $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$ — preserve $C$; those with $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$ act as the identity on $C/y'$; each such $\tau$ acting trivially on $C/y'$ is transported by $e$ to an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ fixing constants and acting on $X_0, X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ by a matrix $M$ congruent to $c\,\gamma$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, with $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, with $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$ and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; primes of $S$ containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ with tangent directions $(a_1{:}b_1)$, $(a_2{:}b_2)$ with $a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ not divisible by $q$ have distinct contractions to the stalk; for a prime $P$ with tangent direction $(1{:}0)$, an element $a \in C$ has germ in the contraction of $P$ exactly when all Laurent coefficients of $a$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$; and [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, differs from some $a_0 \in A$ by an element of $y'$ whose image under $e$ is the class of a power series $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$, $e_0 \ge 1$, whose degree-$e_0$ leading form takes unit values at every pair $(a,b)$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   **The chosen point and its chart presentation.** Specific data $z$, $\varpi_z$ (the germ of $\varpi$, lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk), $y'$ with `ιFin`-image $z$ and satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and `hy'y : y'.asIdeal = y` are given; together with $W_1$, $\sigma_1$, $f_1,u_1,v_1$ (with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$) and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1\bigr)$, the hypothesis `hW₁` being exactly the seven clauses above for this data.
--
--   **The blow-up chart.** $J$ is an ideal of $C$ given by `hJ` as the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $(\tau|_C)^{-1}\bigl((e_1 \circ \text{completion} \circ \text{germ})^{-1}\bigl(\,(\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\,X_0,\,X_1)\,\bigr)\bigr)$, taken over $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. The subalgebra $B$ of $K$ over $A$ is given by `hB` as $C[J/\varpi_t]$: the $C$-subalgebra generated by $\{x \in K : \exists i \in J,\ x\varpi_t = i\}$, viewed as an $A$-subalgebra.
--
--   **The valuation subring and its properties.** $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and: `hR1` states $C \le B$ and that every element of $K$ is a ratio of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2` states that $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that $W \cap L$ is the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ exactly when $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $W$ consists of the ratios $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$; `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) states that for any $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k_A$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k_A`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements of $\mathfrak{m}_W$, compatible with $A \to k_A$ and equivariant for the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, preserving $W$, through elements $(\,$`redQ q γ`$, c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(\gamma,c) \mapsto \det\gamma \cdot c^{q+1}$) acting via [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all these level automorphisms; that every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is hit, in the sense that some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ carry all elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ into $Q$; that any $b \in B$ all of whose such conjugates lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **Further data.** `hjK` and `hjC` place [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) in $K$ and in $C$. The natural number $m \ge 1$ satisfies $\varpi^m = \varpi_t w$ for some unit $w$ of $A$ (`hmt`).
--
--   **Ends.** `ends` is a finite set of subrings of $K$, characterised by `hends`: a subring $O$ lies in `ends` exactly when there are $a \in J \subseteq C$ with $a \ne 0$ in $K$ and, setting $B_a := C[J/a]$ (the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $\{x : \exists i \in J,\ x a = i\}$, viewed over $A$), a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ such that $O$ consists of the ratios $g/h$ with $g,h \in B_a$ and $h \notin P$, such that every $b \in y$ whose image lies in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and such that $B$ is not contained in $O$.
--
--   **The crossing data at the chosen end.** $O \in$ `ends` is given, with $O \subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), $C \subseteq O$ (`hCO`) and $\varpi \in O$ (`hϖO`). Writing $\hat A$ for the $\mathfrak{m}_A$-adic completion of $A$, $\pi$ for the image of $\varpi$ in $\hat A$, and $\mathcal U :=$ `UVCrossingModel` $\hat A\,(\pi^m) = \hat A[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - C(\pi^m))$, the data consist of elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak{m}_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto $\mathcal{U}$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of $\mathcal{U}$, subject to: $c_x c_y = \varpi^m u$ (`hcxy`); $\iota$ sends the image of each $a \in A$ lying in $O$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $a$ in $\hat A$ (`hιc`); $\iota$ sends the image of $c_x$ to $\gamma_U \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.U` $(\pi^m)$ (`hιx`) and the image of $c_y$ to $\gamma_V \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.V` $(\pi^m)$ (`hιy`); and, regarded in $W$, $c_y$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ (`hcyW`) while $c_x$ does not (`hcxW`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists $b \in C =$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` such that $b \in y$ and the image of $b$ in the $\mathfrak{m}_O$-adic completion of $O$, transported by $\iota$, does not lie in the ideal of $\mathcal{U}$ generated by `UVCrossingModel.U` $(\pi^m)$ together with `UVCrossingModel.const` $(\pi^m)\,\pi$.
--
--   At an end $O$ of the blow-up of the supersingular chart, where the completed local ring is a crossing $\hat A[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^m)$, this says that the supersingular maximal ideal $y$ is not contained in the ideal $(U,\varpi)$ cutting out one of the two branches; equivalently, the branch $U = 0$ is not the locus on which all of $y$ vanishes, so it is the strict transform of an Igusa component of the special fibre rather than the exceptional curve. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaBranch_valuationSubring_of_mem_ends_crossing_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaBranch_valuationSubring_of_mem_ends_crossing_linked) to produce the valuation subring of the Igusa branch through the end.
